This is a plain static site with no Jekyll content, so GitHub Pages should
publish the tree exactly as committed rather than running it through a build.

Without this file Pages runs Jekyll, which drops paths it considers its own —
anything under a leading underscore, and `vendor`, where the js-dos runtime and
its WebAssembly emulators live. A missing `vendor/jsdos/player.html` breaks
every DOS game on the deployed site while working perfectly in local testing.
